WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.649 --> 00:00:19.300
ten years ten years is a long time a
decade and in many ways it seems so far

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:34.929
in the past in some ways it doesn't seem
so far away at all it isn't hard to

00:00:34.929 --> 00:00:44.379
remember being deployed in Ramadi Iraq
in the summer of 2006 and yes sometimes

00:00:44.379 --> 00:00:56.260
that seems like a distant place a long
time ago and yet sometimes it feels like

00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:03.100
we were just there yesterday the
sweltering heat the dust the danger the

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:10.090
crystal-clear focus on our mission when
we had but one purpose in our lives to

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:14.979
close with and destroy an evil enemy
bent on destroying us and our way of

00:01:14.979 --> 00:01:26.770
life and it doesn't take much for the
mind to return there to regain that

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:39.159
mindset to get into the combat mode and
remember remember the operations out in

00:01:39.159 --> 00:01:45.820
the city remember the tracer rounds in
the night sky explosions shaking the

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:51.810
earth the weight of body armor and
weapons and gear on our shoulders

00:01:51.810 --> 00:02:00.579
remember the stress and the violence and
the sweat and the blood and remember the

00:02:00.579 --> 00:02:08.379
evil the pure evil
that infected the city and committed

00:02:08.379 --> 00:02:12.470
savage vile and disgusting acts of
mortal

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:26.540
sin murder rape and torture inside that
dark world a world ripped apart by war a

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:36.260
world war sometimes humanity seemed all
but lost that is where we got to see and

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:44.870
experience the polar opposite for the
counter to all that darkness against

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:54.560
that backdrop of evil we young men we
band of brothers

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:59.900
we got to witness light and life and
love so strong that it makes the

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:07.670
darkness fade and makes the evil cower
and hide its wretched face evil boughs

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:12.380
down when it sees the bond we developed
with the soldiers and Marines we fought

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:24.230
alongside evil cannot contest the bond
we formed with our brother SEALs with

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:30.709
whom we become so close that there is no
stronger force in the world nothing more

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:36.400
powerful nothing more meaningful than
knowing that these men these frog men

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:41.709
that we would do anything for each other

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:49.400
we saw powerful acts of heroism and
courage on an almost daily basis which

00:03:49.400 --> 00:04:01.100
reassured us solemnly that good would
triumph over evil and amongst all that

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:09.260
glory there were a few men the true
heroes the ones that rose above the rest

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:23.139
of us to symbolize and personify courage
and faith and selflessness and love mark

00:04:23.139 --> 00:04:32.680
alan lee was one of those rare men one
of those heroes one of the few men my

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:43.689
life that i literally described as a
saint that is who mark was a mighty

00:04:43.689 --> 00:04:50.169
warrior whose ferocity and combat was
perfectly balanced by faith and humor

00:04:50.169 --> 00:04:59.080
and compassion a man that left his mark
on everyone that he met a mark of

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:09.939
happiness and positivity and of humility
and of joy a man whose love for his

00:05:09.939 --> 00:05:17.289
family and friends was so unbounded and
so limitless that you could actually

00:05:17.289 --> 00:05:35.650
feel it emanating from his heart and now
he has left his mark on the world mark

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:42.810
Lee Mark Alan Lee

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:51.440
when faced with fear
who else could bring a smile when faced

00:05:51.440 --> 00:06:00.229
with sadness
who else could bring laughter when faced

00:06:00.229 --> 00:06:02.650
with hate

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:10.669
who else could bring love and when faced
with death

00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:18.199
who else could stand and say take me
Lord not my brothers I will be their

00:06:18.199 --> 00:06:33.310
shield now from death take me and let
them live on and that is what Mark did

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:44.169
full of youth and energy and courage and
humor and full of love

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:52.909
he stood he stood against evil and he
stood against death and he gave his life

00:06:52.909 --> 00:07:15.169
for his brothers and for our freedom on
august 2nd 2006 in our Ramadi Iraq ten

00:07:15.169 --> 00:07:17.800
years ago

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:32.259
ten years ago and in those 10 years
think of all that has happened in our

00:07:32.259 --> 00:07:41.350
lives big events like marriages children
born birthdays new houses new jobs new

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:55.139
careers and small events a morning surf
session lunch with your buddies a

00:07:55.139 --> 00:08:14.070
weekend in the mountains a cold iced tea
on a hot summer's day smile a laugh life

00:08:14.729 --> 00:08:32.950
joy happiness in every moment of that
happiness is a gift

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:46.630
a gift a gift given to us by mark who
sacrificed everything for us who gave up

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:59.380
his own precious smile so we could all
have ours now I can tell you without a

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:05.080
shred of doubt that on this day today
mark would not want tears he would not

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:15.190
want sadness he would not want sorrow he
would want smiles and laughter and joy

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:27.280
because that was his gift to us every
smile every laugh every ounce of life

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:47.620
and love is all a gift from a warrior a
friend a comedian a son a brother a hero

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:54.450
a saint

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:13.550
and what do we owe mark for mark each
and every one of us must relish the gift

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:20.300
that he gave to us and cherish each and
every day while remembering the

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:26.710
incredible man that gave us this gift of

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:48.920
life and to the seals that are listening
the frog men you Oh mark what we owe all

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:56.090
our fallen brothers the grave commitment
to carry the fire to hold the torch and

00:10:56.090 --> 00:11:03.380
hold it high to take the fight to the
enemy every chance you get without mercy

00:11:03.380 --> 00:11:16.330
and without remorse until they are
vanquished and there is peace

00:11:21.339 --> 00:11:28.389
thank you Mark we will never forget you

00:11:28.419 --> 00:11:34.519
god bless Mark's family
god bless the teams god Bless America

00:11:34.519 --> 00:11:41.649
and God bless mark Allan Lee

